A||N||7||Bob Englert||V6 Manifold P/N's???||||1||
Z||000000||Bob Englert||07-21-2001||05:24 PM||||I am looking for the front manifold for my 87 V6.  The Pontiac dealer's parts listings showed #10115725 for the Left Hand manifold and #10115726 for the Right Hand manifold.  He did not know if the front manifold was the RH or LH one.<P>Can anyone tell me which is the correct P/N please?<P>Thanks...<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||07-21-2001||08:45 PM||||The front manifold is the one facing the firewall and the rear is the one facing the trunk.  To figure out which is left or which is right stand in front of the engine with the crank pulley in front of you.  The right manifold is the front one (or the one facing the firewall).  That would mean you need part #10115726.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bob Englert||07-21-2001||09:33 PM||||Thanks Mike.  <P>I obviously knew front and back, but I wasn't sure how to convert that to left and right.  The good news is the front (RH) is cheaper than the rear according to my parts guy at the Pontiac dealership.  He quoted $151 for a RH manifold.  $191 for a LH one.<P>I really think that given all the rain that falls on the front manifold and the age of the car, it makes more sense to go ahead and get a new manifold so I don't have to worry about it for another 12 years or so.  <P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula||07-22-2001||04:10 PM||||I saw a set of new ones in the mall for $200 bucks (both) a while back without any replies, look back a couple of days.||||reg||1
Z||000004||flyntus||07-22-2001||04:49 PM||||Bob,<BR>LivoniaFieroGT has a new set of manifolds for $200 in the PFF Mall.||||reg||1
Z||000005||West Coast Fiero||07-22-2001||05:06 PM||||I was told the stock manifolds were discontinued - this true?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jim Jimenez||07-24-2001||01:09 AM||||The manifolds are not discontinued. I checked on GM tracs system today. There are a few in regional warehouses, the factory warehouses have ample stock. ||||reg||7
Z||000007||88 Database Guy||07-24-2001||08:53 AM||||This is a question for MrFiero.  I would have thought that the front side would be the left side of the engine, and the trunk side would be the right side.  If I had ordered one of these, this is how I would have decided which one to get.  I mean, if the engine was longitudinally oriented, wouldn't the former front side be on the left?  ||||reg||1
